From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:07:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: find the module of an address in a builtin's JIT-pool
 copy

On iOS a builtin's code runs from its JIT-pool copy, so the address of one
of its functions lies in the copy, not in the module's view, and
LdrFindEntryForAddress found no module for it. GetModuleHandleExW with
GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_FROM_ADDRESS then failed with
ERROR_MOD_NOT_FOUND: xgameruntime's WaitTimer names its callback's
module that way for SetThreadpoolCallbackLibrary, so XTaskQueueCreate
failed with 0x8007007e and a GDK game never signed its player in.

LdrFindEntryForAddress now retries a miss with the address
xlate_ios_jit_rev gives, the copy's PE address; any other address is
left alone. The i386 and x86_64 builds do not change.

Linear: PLA-499
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-02-xbox-pilot-task-queue.md
Offered-upstream: no; the JIT pool is the iOS port's
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index f18ebbbc969..993119e3bd8 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -2832,7 +2832,21 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI LdrFindEntryForAddress( const void *addr, PLDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY
     RTL_BALANCED_NODE *node;
 
     if (!(node = rtl_rb_tree_get( &base_address_index_tree, addr, module_address_search_compare )))
+    {
+#if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__arm64ec__)
+        /* iOS: a builtin's code runs from its JIT-pool copy, so the address of
+         * one of its functions (GetModuleHandleExW's FROM_ADDRESS, a threadpool
+         * callback library) lies in the copy, not in the module's view.
+         * xlate_ios_jit_rev turns it into its PE address and leaves any other
+         * address alone. */
+        extern void *xlate_ios_jit_rev( void *ptr );
+        const void *pe = xlate_ios_jit_rev( (void *)addr );
+
+        if (!pe || pe == addr ||
+            !(node = rtl_rb_tree_get( &base_address_index_tree, pe, module_address_search_compare )))
+#endif
         return STATUS_NO_MORE_ENTRIES;
+    }
     *pmod = CONTAINING_RECORD(node, LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY, BaseAddressIndexNode);
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
